SUMMARY:ROM Discounted - Tour\, World Wildlife Photography + Other Exhibit
 s
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nOn **Saturday November 21st\,** **join me 
 at the Royal Ontario Museum (ROM) to take a Museum Tour\, visit the World 
 Wildlife Photography Exhibit\, the Crawford Lake Exhibit and Cloudscape In
 stallation.** Be among the first in Canada to see this year’s winners an
 d finalists of the annual *[Wildlife Photographer of the Year](https://www
 .rom.on.ca/whats-on/exhibitions/wildlife-photographer-year-2026)* 2026 com
 petition. Attendees can see any exhibits of interest. **Purchase your tick
 et for Saturday November 21st. We will be heading out for dinner after at 
 the number 1 Chinese restaurant in Canada. This is a separate event and yo
 u can sign up [here](https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/31686
 9554/) if you'd like to join us.**\n\n**Museum Highlights Tour**\nExplore 
 the wonders of ROM in a 45-minute tour that brings iconic objects to life.
  Enjoy highlights of arts\, culture and nature… throughout the world and
  throughout time.\n\n**Cloudscape Installation**\n*Cloudscape* is a mesmer
 izing installation that blends traditional artistry with contemporary them
 es. Immerse yourself in Yan's floating masterpiece\, where each sculpted c
 loud tells a story of cultural heritage and environmental consciousness\, 
 and invites us to reflect on our relationship with nature.\n\n**World Wild
 life Photography**\nEach year\, the annual competition - organized by the 
 Natural History Museum in London\, UK - receives tens of thousands of imag
 e submissions from aspiring wildlife photographers of all ages. One hundre
 d selected images from this year's competition - unforgettable photographs
  of wildlife and the natural world - will travel to ROM right after the wi
 nners are announced. Experience the power of photography to reveal\, conne
 ct\, and transform our view of nature.\n\n**Itinerary**\n**2:30pm Meet ins
 ide the ROM at the Museum Station entrance** to the right side on the 1st 
 Floor\n\n**2:35 - 2:45pm Cloudscape Installation** (**Level 1 China(**\n\n
 **2:45 - 3:45pm Museum Highlights Tour (Level 1 Currelle Gallery)**. The T
 our starts 3pm\, then head directly to the Wildlife Exhibit to enter befor
 e 4pm.\n\n**3:45 - 4:45pm World Wildlife Photography Exhibit\, Level 4\, P
 atrick Harris Gallery (last entry 4pm)**\n\n**4:45pm - 4:55pm Break**\n\n*
 *4:55 -** **5:15p Crawford Lake Exhibit (Level 3\, European Rotating Exhib
 itions)**\nPowerful\, inspiring\, and enlightening\, the annual Wildlife P
 hotographer of the Year exhibition invites viewers into a world of extraor
 dinary images and visual storytelling. The world's longest-running and mos
 t prestigious annual nature photography competition\, Wildlife Photographe
 r of the Year attracts and recognizes the world's best nature photography\
 , and has done so every year since 1965.\n\n**5:15 - 5:25pm: ROM Store.** 
 Take a look around for souvenirs.\n\n**5:30pm Museum closes**\n**We will b
 e heading out for dinner at the number 1 Chinese restaurant in Canada. Sig
 n up [here](https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/316869554/) if
  you'd like to join us.**\n\n**COST**\nAdults: Admission $26 + Photography
  Exhibit $9 = $35\nSeniors: Admission $21 + Photography Exhibit = $27.75\n
 \nDiscounted 15% (message me for the code)\nAdults: Admission only is $22.
 10\, Admission + Photography is $29.75\n\nSeniors: Admission only is $17.8
 5\, Admission + Photography is $23.59\n\nMeetup fee: $5\n\n***\n\n**SIGNIN
 G-UP**\n\n* **Simply RSVP Yes (everyone goes on the waitlist until they po
 st they have purchased their ticket).**\n* **[Purchase](https://tickets.ro
 m.on.ca/en/shop) your ticket by selecting Saturday November 21st\, General
  Admission plus World Wildlife Photography\, 10am - 4pm\, and complete the
  transaction. Please post you have your ticket\, and I will move you to at
 tending. If you would like the discount code\, please message me.**\n* RSV
 Ps close 1 day prior\, and cancellations after will result in a No Show an
 d impact future attendance.\n* You can also just show up and join us at th
 e event meetup spot and time\n* A reminder will go out the day before with
  my cell and details when to meet\, etc.\n\n‐‐----‐----‐‐-------
 ------‐-----------\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet members at 2:30pm** **inside
  the entrance of the ROM at the Museum Station Entrance on Queen's Park Av
 enue to the right side**\n\nWe will follow the itinerary above: however\, 
 folks can choose which other exhibits to visit\, understanding there may b
 e an additional cost.\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments after!
